{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And the generation shall say, etc., and they shall see, etc.</b> It is difficult why He placed the saying before the seeing, since it is about the seeing that they speak — for He should have said ״וְרָאוּ הַדּוֹר הָאַחֲרוֹן״ וְגוֹ׳ ״וְהַנָּכְרִי״ וְגוֹ׳ ״וְאָמְרוּ״ וְגוֹ׳. And moreover, there was no need to say ״וְאָמַר״ וְגוֹ׳, since afterward He says ״וְאָמְרוּ״ וְגוֹ׳. Further, why did He begin speaking in singular and finish saying ״וְאָמְרוּ״ in plural — ״וְאָמְרוּ כָּל הַגּוֹיִם״?" "<b>And it appears</b> that the verse's intention is along this line: ״וְאָמַר הַדּוֹר הָאַחֲרוֹן״ — that is, the generation that is among your children, and it was necessary to specify because there are generations among the nations. And not he alone said it, but also ״הַנָּכְרִי אֲשֶׁר יָבֹא״ וְגוֹ׳ — meaning the nearby foreigner and also the one who comes from a far land — as if it said ״וַאֲשֶׁר יָבֹא״ וְגוֹ׳. ״וְרָאוּ״ — meaning those foreigners, near and far, ״אֶת מַכּוֹת הָאָרֶץ״ וְגוֹ׳. ״וְאָמְרוּ כָּל הַגּוֹיִם״ — they too, in addition to the statement of the last generation ״בְּנֵיכֶם״ וְגוֹ׳, ״עַל מֶה עָשָׂה״ וְגוֹ׳. And He mentioned ״וְרָאוּ״ regarding the foreigners but not regarding the last generation among their children, because the latter are present in the land of Israel and see what is done, and there was no need to say of them ״וְרָאוּ״. And His saying ״כָּל הַגּוֹיִם״ — the verse informs that those who see will tell everyone what HaShem has wondrously done in that city." "<b>And all</b> of this statement corresponds to the first division that the verse mentioned: ״פֶּן יֵשׁ בָּכֶם אִישׁ״ וְגוֹ׳ ״אוֹ מִשְׁפָּחָה אוֹ שֵׁבֶט״ וְגוֹ׳ ״לָלֶכֶת לַעֲבֹד״ וְגוֹ׳ — because the curses he specified until now were against the second division, ״בַּעַל שֹׁרֶשׁ פֹּרֶה רֹאשׁ וְלַעֲנָה,״ and He has already blotted out his name from under the heavens. From here He begins the punishment of the first one: ״וְרָאוּ אֶת מַכּוֹת״ וְגוֹ׳." "And His saying <b>עַל אֲשֶׁר עָזְבוּ</b> וְגוֹ׳, <b>וַיֵּלְכוּ וַיַּעַבְדוּ</b> וְגוֹ׳ — as it says at the beginning of the passage: ״לָלֶכֶת לַעֲבֹד.״ Therefore He did not say ״וּמָחָה ה׳ אֶת שְׁמָם,״ but rather desolated their land and exiled them from upon their soil and cast them into another land וְגוֹ׳."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:20:22.035833467Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}